## Counting from 0:  this project's lists start at 0 (its project file)
// Numbers count from 0;  ordinal words don't change.  Its rack is its own:  five tiles, A first.
a "tile" is a thing where:
	- its "letter" is text

a "rack" is a list of tiles where:
	// a new rack holds five tiles, A to E
	- to create it:
		add (a new tile with letter = "A") to the rack
		add (a new tile with letter = "B") to the rack
		add (a new tile with letter = "C") to the rack
		add (a new tile with letter = "D") to the rack
		add (a new tile with letter = "E") to the rack


## Tests
to test counting from zero
	the rack is a new rack
	the letter of tile 0 of the rack should be "A"
	the letter of tile 1 of the rack should be "B"
	the letter of tile -1 of the rack should be "E"
	the letter of the first tile of the rack should be "A"
	the letter of the second tile of the rack should be "B"
	the letter of the last tile of the rack should be "E"
	set the start to the first tile of the rack
	the position of the start in the rack should be 0
	set the front to tiles 0 to 2 of the rack
	the number of tiles in the front should be 3
	the letter of the last tile of the front should be "C"
	set the back to last two tiles of the rack
	the number of tiles in the back should be 2
	the letter of the first tile of the back should be "D"
	set the positions to a new list of numbers
	for each tile, position in the front
		add position to the positions
	echo "positions: " + the positions
	remove tile 0 of the rack
	the letter of the first tile of the rack should be "B"
